@startuml
title E04 - Hub/cloud/app connectivity and freshness
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Primary caregiver" as Caregiver
boundary "A05\nApp platform" as A05
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
control "B07\nRead models/API" as B07
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
H08 -> B08: Send heartbeat/cloud receipt when connected
B08 -> B08: Evaluate hub lease using server receipt time
Caregiver -> A05: Open/refresh application
A05 -> B07: GET snapshot with client request time
B07 -> B08: Read independent hub health and diagnostics
B07 --> A05: Return fetched-at, last hub receipt and last activity separately
A05 -> A05: Classify network/auth/service failure and cache version
A05 -> A02: Build independent phone, API, hub and activity freshness labels
A02 -> Caregiver: Display explicit stale/offline/never-seen states
note over H08,A02: A fresh API response does not make a stale hub current, and activity freshness is a separate dimension.
note over Caregiver,A02: Outcome - Each connectivity boundary and evidence timestamp remains separately visible so the family knows what is actually known.
@enduml
